22::
0:
System

10:
Em stop state active\n
Em stop reset is required.\n
Press the panel button.\n
\t\n

11:
Em stop state active\n
Em stop reset is required.\n
First release the Em stop button\n
and then press the panel button.\n
\t\n

12:
Sys failure state active\n
Fatal non recoverable system error.\n
Warm start is required.\n
\t\n
Switch the mains switch off and on\n
again if the soft restart command is\n
ignored or not possible to reach.


24:
Enable chain timeout\n
Two channel status timeout.\n
\t\n
The acknowledgement for a two channel\n
enable chain status change was not\n
received within the expected time.


30:
Axis not commutated\n
One or several internal drive unit\n
axes are not commutated.\n
\t\n

31:
Axis not calibrated\n
One or several absolute/relative\n
measurement axes are not calibrated.\n
\t\n

32:
Rev counter not updated\n
One or several absolute measurement\n
axes are not synchronized.\n
\n
Move the robot to the sync position\n
and update the revolution counters.\n
\t\n

33:
Axis not synchronized\n
One or several relative measurement\n
axes are not synchronized.\n
\n
Order Motors On and synchronize all\n
mechanical units in the list.\n
\t\n

50:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed in this operating mode.\n
\t\n

51:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed when client not in control\n
of the resource (program/motion).\n
\t\n

52:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed in this cabinet state.\n
\t\n

53:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed in this manipulator state.\n
\t\n

54:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed when program is executing.\n
\t\n

60:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed in Auto mode.\n
\t\n

61:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed when changing to Auto mode.\n
\t\n

62:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed in Manual mode.\n
\t\n

63:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed in Manual full speed mode.\n
\t\n

64:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed when changing to Manual\n
full speed mode.\n
\t\n

70:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed in Motors On state.\n
\t\n

71:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed while changing to\n
Motors On state.\n
\t\n

72:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed in Motors Off state.\n
\t\n

73:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed while changing to\n
Motors Off state.\n
\t\n

74:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed in Guard Stop state.\n
\t\n

75:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed in Emergency Stop state.\n
\n
Em stop reset is required.\n
Press the panel button.\n
\t\n

76:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed in System Failure state.\n
\n
Fatal non recoverable system error.\n
Warm start is required.\n
\t\n
Switch the mains switch off and on\n
again if the soft restart command is\n
ignored or not possible to reach.

80:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed when axis is not commutated.\n
\t\n

81:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed when axis is not calibrated.\n
\t\n

82:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed when axis rev counter is not\n
updated.\n
\t\n

83:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed when axis is not\n
synchronized.\n
\t\n

92:
Not allowed command\n
Not allowed in state\n
System IO Start Blocked.\n
\t\n

100:
Teachpendant in ctrl\n
A teachpendant application\n
is in control of the requested\n
resource (program/motion)\n
\t\n

101:
Teachp (prg) in ctrl\n
The teachpendant programming\n
window has focus and is in control\n
of the program server.\n
Change to the production window\n
and perform the command again.\n
\t\n

102:
Teachp (joystick) in ctrl\n
The teachpendant joystick is in\n
control of the motion server.\n
Release the joystick and perform\n
the command again.\n
\t\n

111:
Teachp (prg) in ctrl\n
The teachpendant programming\n
window has focus and is in control\n
of the program server.\n
Change to the production window\n
and perform the command again.\n
\t\n

112:
Program 1 in ctrl\n
The program server 1 is in\n
control of the motion server.\n
Stop the program and perform\n
the command again.\n
\t\n

113:
Program 2 in ctrl\n
The program server 2 is\n
in control of the motion server.\n
Stop the program and perform\n
the command again.\n
\t\n

114:
Program 3 in ctrl\n
The program server 3 is\n
in control of the motion server.\n
Stop the program and perform\n
the command again.\n
\t\n

115:
Program 4 in ctrl\n
The program server 4 is\n
in control of the motion server.\n
Stop the program and perform\n
the command again.\n
\t\n

116:
Program 5 in ctrl\n
The program server 5 is\n
in control of the motion server.\n
Stop the program and perform\n
the command again.\n
\t\n

120:
System IO in ctrl\n
\t\n

125:
Client %s in ctrl\n
Specified client is in\n
control of the requested\n
resource (program/motion)\n
\t\n

130:
Out of memory in cfg\n
\t\n

131:
Unable to read file\n
\t\n

132:
Parameters not saved\n
Parameters cannot be saved.\n
Probably, because disk is write\n
protected or no space available.\n
\t\n
Check if disk is write-protected or\n
if space on disk is enough.

133:
Cannot modify instance\n
Description\Reason:\n
Can't replace instance in line %d\n
of file %s\n
\t\n
The instance is write protected.

134:
Wrong version\n
Description\Reason:\n
The cfg domain version is wrong in file\n
%s\n
The software is made for\n
version %s\n
\t\n
Change the version of the cfg domain.

135:
Line too long\n
Description\Reason:\n
Line %d > %d characters\n
\t\n
Reduce the number of characters.

136:
Attr out of range\n
Description\Reason:\n
Attribute %s is out of range\n
in line %d\n
\t\n
Change the value on the attribute.

137:
Dublicate inst name\n
Description\Reason:\n
Dublicate name in line %d\n
of file %s\n
\t\n
Change the name.

140:
Motors On rejected.\n
Motors On via System IO\n
not allowed.\n
\t\n

141:
Motors Off rejected.\n
Motors Off via System IO\n
not allowed.\n
\t\n

142:
Start rejected.\n
Start/restart of program via System\n
IO not allowed.\n
\t\n
The reason could be that the robot\n
is outside of regain distance.

143:
Start main rejected.\n
Start of main program via System IO\n
not allowed.\n
\t\n

144:
Stop rejected.\n
Stop of program via System IO\n
not allowed.\n
\t\n

145:
Stop cycle rejected.\n
Stop of program cycle via System IO\n
not allowed.\n
\t\n

146:
Man interrupt rejected.\n
Manual interrupt of program via\n
System IO not allowed.\n
\t\n

147:
Load and start rejected.\n
Load and start of program via\n
System IO not allowed.\n
Program file name (including mass\n
memory unit) to be loaded must\n
be defined.\n
\t\n

148:
Confirm rejected.\n
Emergency Stop Reset Confirm via\n
System IO not allowed.\n
\t\n

149:
Error reset rejected.\n
Program execution error reset via\n
System IO not allowed.\n
\t\n

150:
Syncronization rejected.\n
Syncronization of mechanical unit\n
via System IO not allowed.\n
\t\n

151:
Faulty signal name.\n
Signal name not possible to\n
subscribe to for Sysio.\n
The Signal name might not be in\n
the cfg-file for Sysio.\n
\t\n

152:
Too many restrictions.\n
For an action (signal) in\n
Sysio, no restrictions are set.\n
The total number of restrictions\n
(signals) for an action in the\n
cfg-file for Sysio are too high.\n
\t\n

153:
Mot. On, Start rejected.\n
Motors On, Start/restart of program\n
via System IO not allowed.\n
\t\n
The reason could be that the robot\n
is outside of regain distance.

154:
Stop instr. rejected.\n
Stop of program instruction via\n
System IO not allowed.\n
\t\n

155:
Undefined Argument\n
SyncExtAx mechanical_unit_name\n
is not defined\n
\t\n

156:
Undefined Argument\n
Interrupt routine_name\n
is not defined\n
\t\n

157:
Undefined Argument\n
LoadStart program_name\n
is not defined\n
\t\n

158:
No System Input signal\n
A system input has been declared to\n
a signal that doesnt exist.\n
\t\n

159:
No System Output signal\n
A system output has been declared to\n
a signal that doesnt exist.\n
\t\n

160:
Not in configuration\n
The system module %!%s in task\n
%s has no corresponding\n
specification in the configuration\n
for "Task modules"\n
\t\n
View "Task modules" in the "System\n
Parameter" menu and add an item for\n
this system module

161:
Path not find\n
The system module %!%s in task\n
%s has a corresponding\n
specification in the configuration\n
for "Task modules" that point out\n
a non existing file path\n
\t\n
View "Task modules" in the "System\n
Parameter" menu and change the path\n
in the item for this system module

162:
Write error\n
A write error occur when the system try\n
to save the system module %!%.14s\n
at %.37s\n
in task %.16s. Or the file\n
system was full\n
\t\n
View "Task modules" in the "System\n
Parameter" menu and change the path\n
in the item for this system module

163:
Reconfig failed\n
Some user module(s) changed but not\n
saved. See previous warnings stored\n
in the log.\n
\t\n
Save those modules that are specified\n
by earlier warnings and try another\n
system start.

164:
Reconfig failed\n
There are still some unsaved system\n
module\n
\t\n
Read error descriptions in earlier\n
messages.\n
Try another system start

165:
PP lost!\n
Restart is no longer possible from\n
current position. The program has to be\n
started from the beginning.\n
\t\n

166:
Refuse to save module\n
The module %!%.14s\n
is older than the source\n
at %.37s\n
in task %.16s.\n
\t\n

167:
Unsaved module\n
The module %!%.14s\n
is changed but not saved\n
in task %.16s.\n
\t\n

170:
SYS_STOP\n
Program motion stopped along path.\n
\t\n

171:
SYS_HALT\n
Program and motion stopped with\n
motors off.\n
\t\n

172:
SYS_FAIL\n
System Failure, restart system.\n
\t\n

175:
Teachpendant fail\n
Teachpendant lost contact\n
this will force Guard Stop\n
\t\n

180:
System IO restriction\n
System IO restrictions are active for\n
other clients, e.g. teach pendant or\n
computer link.\n
\t\n
Motor on is restricted by System IO\n
MotorOff.\n
Program start is restricted by\n
System IO Stop, StopCycle or StopInstr.

261:
Strings to long\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Elog message number %d:\n
  Total String length %d >\n
  %d characters\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Reduce the total string length.

270:
Access error\n
Panel Module access error.\n
\t\n
Examine your EIO configuration files.

280:
Symbol conflict\n
The signal %s defined in the IO\n
configuration conflict with another\n
program symbol with the same name.\n
Due on that fact the signal will not be\n
mapped to a program variable.\n
\t\n
Rename the signal in\n
the IO configuration.

313:
SoftStop\n
SoftStop has been detected on\n
channel %.0f.\n
\t\n
Em button has been pressed with\n
SoftStop activated. This will open\n
runchain. Make sure the Em button is\n
reset and press the panel button.\n













